1
00:00:15,660 --> 00:00:24,719
Q: Can you describe the Four Noble Truths

2
00:00:24,720 --> 00:00:28,979
that the Buddha teaches? Suffering, is

3
00:00:28,980 --> 00:00:32,489
the First Noble Truth, there is suffering, second,

4
00:00:32,490 --> 00:00:36,149
there is the cause of suffering. 3rd, cessation of

5
00:00:36,150 --> 00:00:41,099
suffering and 4th, Path leading to the cessation of suffering.

6
00:00:41,100 --> 00:00:44,579
A: Well, first and foremost,

7
00:00:44,580 --> 00:00:47,699
they are 4 descriptions, or

8
00:00:47,700 --> 00:00:53,469
four aspects of one insight, that insight being freedom

9
00:00:53,470 --> 00:00:57,280
from suffering basically, feel free from suffering,

10
00:00:57,780 --> 00:00:58,369
that already implies

11
00:00:58,370 --> 00:01:00,079
the knowledge of what suffering is,

12
00:01:00,080 --> 00:01:01,959
that already implies

13
00:01:01,960 --> 00:01:04,139
the knowledge of what has been causing

14
00:01:04,140 --> 00:01:07,679
that suffering, that already implies the knowledge of freedom from suffering

15
00:01:07,680 --> 00:01:16,029
and that already implies the knowledge of how to maintain, that freedom from suffering, that insight.

16
00:01:16,030 --> 00:01:16,709
Q: How to develop it?

17
00:01:16,710 --> 00:01:20,659
A: well, how to maintain, which basically then

18
00:01:20,660 --> 00:01:22,579
results in complete Liberation

19
00:01:22,580 --> 00:01:31,489
from all the Upakkilesa and all the other kinds of pollution.

20
00:01:31,490 --> 00:01:35,689
So it's not like 1, 2, 3, 4 that the person needs to discern

21
00:01:35,690 --> 00:01:36,399
one by one,

22
00:01:36,400 --> 00:01:41,909
basically, suffering and freedom from it.

23
00:01:41,910 --> 00:01:44,749
And that's what many suttas mention

24
00:01:44,750 --> 00:01:47,069
basically. It would only

25
00:01:47,070 --> 00:01:51,169
talk about the cause of suffering.

26
00:01:51,170 --> 00:01:56,809
Cause of suffering is, Nothing else except Craving

27
00:01:56,810 --> 00:01:58,589
and that's again,

28
00:01:58,590 --> 00:02:04,729
that's something that people might read over, and it seems like

29
00:02:04,730 --> 00:02:06,429
it's making sense of course

30
00:02:06,430 --> 00:02:09,719
But actually, in terms of the direct insight,

31
00:02:09,720 --> 00:02:11,679
seeing the craving is suffering

32
00:02:11,680 --> 00:02:15,959
results in Liberation from that suffering Seeing

33
00:02:15,960 --> 00:02:16,769
the craving, means

34
00:02:16,770 --> 00:02:19,649
abandoning the craving, so the only reason you crave, is

35
00:02:19,650 --> 00:02:21,059
you don't really see it,

36
00:02:21,060 --> 00:02:22,409
directly you don't understand it,

37
00:02:22,410 --> 00:02:28,089
you haven't discerned it. And

38
00:02:28,090 --> 00:02:29,999
important aspect is to recognize that

39
00:02:30,000 --> 00:02:38,939
whenever there is suffering present, you can induce correctly,

40
00:02:38,940 --> 00:02:40,569
that the craving must be present

41
00:02:40,570 --> 00:02:43,739
because suffering is there.

42
00:02:43,740 --> 00:02:48,779
So it's not like, ''oh I suffer, now I have to look for the reason'', call it

43
00:02:48,780 --> 00:02:52,869
craving or something else or also assuming that sometimes, something else can be

44
00:02:52,870 --> 00:02:55,259
the cause of your suffering.

45
00:02:55,260 --> 00:02:57,069
Really needs to be brought down so narrowly

46
00:02:57,070 --> 00:02:59,009
and so precisely

47
00:02:59,010 --> 00:03:02,799
whereby you discern when the suffering, the disagreeable

48
00:03:02,800 --> 00:03:04,739
unpleasant feeling that you are resisting

49
00:03:04,740 --> 00:03:06,659
basically, when the suffering is present,

50
00:03:06,660 --> 00:03:07,439
means, it's because

51
00:03:07,440 --> 00:03:11,479
simultaneously with it, there is craving present.

52
00:03:11,480 --> 00:03:13,949
The absence of the craving, simultaneously means

53
00:03:13,950 --> 00:03:15,259
the absence of that suffering,

54
00:03:15,260 --> 00:03:17,329
there is no delay. That's why

55
00:03:17,330 --> 00:03:20,009
you can have the direct knowledge of freedom

56
00:03:20,010 --> 00:03:23,709
from suffering, directly verified for yourself.

57
00:03:23,710 --> 00:03:27,189
You cannot suffer amid suffering as the Buddha

58
00:03:27,190 --> 00:03:28,429
would often say,

59
00:03:28,430 --> 00:03:31,839
literally amid the things that used to make you suffer,

60
00:03:31,840 --> 00:03:34,129
the mind cannot suffer now

61
00:03:34,130 --> 00:03:40,769
because there is no more craving in regard to those things.

62
00:03:40,770 --> 00:03:41,819
Q: How to abandon craving?

63
00:03:41,820 --> 00:03:48,809
A: How to abandon craving? Well, sense restraint,

64
00:03:48,810 --> 00:03:53,859
Virtue, developed to the extent necessary, whereby you start

65
00:03:53,860 --> 00:03:56,749
discerning then, your mental intentions,

66
00:03:56,750 --> 00:03:59,139
whether they're rooted in wholesome

67
00:03:59,140 --> 00:04:02,479
unwholesome, whether they're rooted in greed aversion, delusion.

68
00:04:02,480 --> 00:04:03,809
And when you know that they are,

69
00:04:03,810 --> 00:04:06,739
you do not engage in them, you do not tolerate them, you do not

70
00:04:06,740 --> 00:04:07,679
entertain them, you do not

71
00:04:07,680 --> 00:04:11,589
proliferate them, you do not invest in them.

72
00:04:11,590 --> 00:04:14,039
That would basically enable the mind to then

73
00:04:14,040 --> 00:04:16,529
Not resist the unpleasant

74
00:04:16,530 --> 00:04:19,909
feeling, to Not indulge the pleasant

75
00:04:19,910 --> 00:04:22,939
feeling, to Not try to distract yourself

76
00:04:22,940 --> 00:04:26,319
from neutral feeling. And when mind stops doing

77
00:04:26,320 --> 00:04:28,839
that, with the previous knowledge

78
00:04:28,840 --> 00:04:32,629
that he's heard from outside through the suttas and right teaching.

79
00:04:32,630 --> 00:04:34,839
when mind stops doing that,

80
00:04:34,840 --> 00:04:37,509
with the previous knowledge of what craving is,

81
00:04:37,510 --> 00:04:39,299
to be able to see, ''ah this is the absence of craving''

82
00:04:39,300 --> 00:04:42,819
and he will be able to see right there, ''ah there is no suffering''

83
00:04:42,820 --> 00:04:48,199
And then you'll be also able to understand what that

84
00:04:48,200 --> 00:04:50,819
suffering was, even the suffering of the past.

85
00:04:50,820 --> 00:04:53,529
Before he understood the way out,

86
00:04:53,530 --> 00:04:56,409
he wouldn't be suffering on account of that either.

87
00:04:56,410 --> 00:04:57,799
The same knowledge would be applied to

88
00:04:57,800 --> 00:05:00,770
the present, past and future.

89
00:05:10,770 --> 00:05:17,849
Q: How to endure those painful feelings

90
00:05:17,850 --> 00:05:22,199
you have them now?

91
00:05:22,200 --> 00:05:23,009
A: You endure them

92
00:05:23,010 --> 00:05:25,339
basically, instead of enduring,

93
00:05:25,340 --> 00:05:27,859
you want to give in to sensuality

94
00:05:27,860 --> 00:05:30,209
or you want to give in to ill-will or distraction.

95
00:05:30,210 --> 00:05:31,429
Well, you don't do that.

96
00:05:31,430 --> 00:05:33,889
Then, that would result in you having to endure them

97
00:05:33,890 --> 00:05:36,079
but sometimes if you can,

98
00:05:36,080 --> 00:05:38,869
you don't have to endure them

99
00:05:38,870 --> 00:05:42,489
without having to give in to sensuality, aversion or delusion

100
00:05:42,490 --> 00:05:43,759
then, that's fine as well.

101
00:05:43,760 --> 00:05:45,429
So you don't have to just constantly going

102
00:05:45,430 --> 00:05:46,649
looking for pain, to endure

103
00:05:46,650 --> 00:05:50,820
that wouldn't necessarily result in wisdom.

104
00:06:01,810 --> 00:06:05,390
Q: Then how does one know if you're free from craving?

105
00:06:06,270 --> 00:06:12,719
A: Because there's no suffering amidst suffering. There is no suffering because you CANNOT suffer.

106
00:06:12,720 --> 00:06:14,319
Not because you're hiding away from it

107
00:06:14,320 --> 00:06:16,359
or because you're not

108
00:06:16,360 --> 00:06:20,079
just avoiding things that used to

109
00:06:20,080 --> 00:06:22,179
cause you to suffer, No.

110
00:06:22,180 --> 00:06:25,119
Because avoiding things means you're afraid of something already.

111
00:06:25,120 --> 00:06:28,649
A person doesn't leave a kuti

112
00:06:28,650 --> 00:06:29,859
then, they don't have to talk to anyone

113
00:06:29,860 --> 00:06:32,239
because it might annoy them and then suffer.

114
00:06:32,240 --> 00:06:33,999
So they aren't free from suffering,

115
00:06:34,000 --> 00:06:38,679
they're just protecting their precarious environment of non-disturbance.

116
00:06:38,680 --> 00:06:40,049
But the fact that you must protect it,

117
00:06:40,050 --> 00:06:42,119
means you're disturbed by that,

118
00:06:42,120 --> 00:06:48,069
which means they're not truly Not suffering, they're just hiding away from the greater extent of it

119
00:06:48,070 --> 00:06:48,979
So you want to recognize it. That's why

120
00:06:48,980 --> 00:06:54,199
Conscientious man doesn't neglect his duty, certain things that you must do,

121
00:06:54,200 --> 00:06:56,449
they're not necessarily connected,

122
00:06:56,450 --> 00:06:59,419
just sitting in solitude and practising

123
00:06:59,420 --> 00:07:02,959
like here, we live by ourselves, we do things ourselves

124
00:07:02,960 --> 00:07:06,280
so we have to go and fix the water line.

125
00:07:07,430 --> 00:07:08,539
I don't have to,

126
00:07:08,540 --> 00:07:12,929
but then I won't have any water.

127
00:07:12,930 --> 00:07:14,569
But having to do that, doesn't bother you either.

128
00:07:14,570 --> 00:07:18,199
You're not seeking out as a distraction,

129
00:07:18,200 --> 00:07:19,389
but you're not running away from it

130
00:07:19,390 --> 00:07:20,569
when it arises on its own

131
00:07:20,570 --> 00:07:21,189
as something that's

132
00:07:21,190 --> 00:07:28,179
necessary to be done to sustain the way you live in.

133
00:07:28,180 --> 00:07:30,649
So you need to have again, that self-honesty,

134
00:07:30,650 --> 00:07:31,079
So you know,

135
00:07:31,080 --> 00:07:32,069
you're not hiding away.

136
00:07:32,070 --> 00:07:32,939
You're not indulging,

137
00:07:32,940 --> 00:07:37,389
you're not covering anything up, with that self-honesty, and restraint

138
00:07:37,390 --> 00:07:38,829
of the senses, seeing the danger in slightest fault,

139
00:07:38,830 --> 00:07:41,329
moderation in eating,

140
00:07:41,330 --> 00:07:41,889
they'll result in

141
00:07:41,890 --> 00:07:44,829
just obviously being mindful of your actions.

142
00:07:44,830 --> 00:07:48,840
You start discerning mental Intentions, by discerning them

143
00:07:48,980 --> 00:07:52,159
basically, mind is already developing certain perspective

144
00:07:52,160 --> 00:07:55,999
because there is no craving without intention.

145
00:07:56,000 --> 00:07:58,329
But there is intention without craving.

146
00:07:58,330 --> 00:08:01,809
That's why Arahant still can intend and decide and choose

147
00:08:01,810 --> 00:08:04,199
but he has no craving.

148
00:08:04,200 --> 00:08:07,699
But in order to see that, you have to see the intentions

149
00:08:07,700 --> 00:08:08,539
to begin with,

150
00:08:08,540 --> 00:08:11,609
most people are not even aware of the mental intentions.

151
00:08:11,610 --> 00:08:14,689
They think intention is just the most obvious choice,

152
00:08:14,690 --> 00:08:15,289
but it's not,

153
00:08:15,290 --> 00:08:17,629
it's just little inclinations, thoughts in themselves

154
00:08:17,630 --> 00:08:21,149
are already intentional.

155
00:08:21,150 --> 00:08:23,629
So it's subtler, and in order to reach the subtler level,

156
00:08:23,630 --> 00:08:27,369
this whole sense restraint, restrained by Patimokkha

157
00:08:27,370 --> 00:08:29,439
by virtue, moderation

158
00:08:29,440 --> 00:08:36,459
in eating, mindfulness, is absolutely necessary, not negotiable. And with right instructions, and right way of

159
00:08:36,460 --> 00:08:37,649
looking, that's where the practice is.

160
00:08:37,650 --> 00:08:40,169
Without the right instruction,

161
00:08:40,170 --> 00:08:42,309
it is just restraint, which is good,

162
00:08:42,310 --> 00:08:49,209
but it doesn't lead you to any knowledge, but with the right instruction and that, that's all you need.

163
00:08:49,210 --> 00:08:50,539
Because sometimes people might think,

164
00:08:50,540 --> 00:08:53,649
OK, restraint is not the Dhamma, that's true

165
00:08:53,650 --> 00:08:55,839
and then they'd think, ''Ok now, I got the Dhamma

166
00:08:55,840 --> 00:08:57,209
so I don't have to restrain'', No.

167
00:08:57,210 --> 00:09:02,069
Dhamma applies only where the restraint is.

168
00:09:02,070 --> 00:09:03,519
So, you can see.

169
00:09:03,520 --> 00:09:06,019
Yes, Restraint is not the Dhamma, as in the application of

170
00:09:06,020 --> 00:09:10,819
dhamma, is not the same as the necessary basis for the application,

171
00:09:10,820 --> 00:09:11,699
but you wouldn't be able to apply it

172
00:09:11,700 --> 00:09:17,989
if there is no necessary basis.

173
00:09:17,990 --> 00:09:20,509
And if the mind practises like that,

174
00:09:20,510 --> 00:09:24,239
then, the inclination

175
00:09:24,240 --> 00:09:27,219
in form of craving, is becoming more and more obvious.

176
00:09:27,220 --> 00:09:31,639
Why? Because you start recognizing that certain ways

177
00:09:31,640 --> 00:09:33,379
when you intend and incline,

178
00:09:33,380 --> 00:09:38,189
makes you suffer, makes you feel too much, so to speak.

179
00:09:38,190 --> 00:09:41,999
Makes you too involved, exposes you,

180
00:09:42,000 --> 00:09:43,999
makes you liable,

181
00:09:44,000 --> 00:09:46,450
by discerning those things, you stop intending like that.

182
00:09:51,300 --> 00:09:57,510
By not intending like that, you're not perpetuating the craving.

183
00:10:04,190 --> 00:10:10,299
Q: In terms of feelings?

184
00:10:10,300 --> 00:10:14,370
A: Yes, of course, it's always in relation to feelings.

185
00:10:19,370 --> 00:10:26,249
So in an agreeable feeling, that is present,

186
00:10:26,250 --> 00:10:29,569
you have to

187
00:10:29,570 --> 00:10:34,359
discern the inclination

188
00:10:34,360 --> 00:10:35,469
towards wanting more of it

189
00:10:35,470 --> 00:10:36,869
or towards wanting to stay longer,

190
00:10:36,870 --> 00:10:39,529
towards wanting to not go away soon,

191
00:10:39,530 --> 00:10:40,899
towards wanting to increase it,

192
00:10:40,900 --> 00:10:43,139
to intensify it, to prolong it,

193
00:10:43,140 --> 00:10:48,299
any of those things. In a disagreeable feeling,

194
00:10:48,300 --> 00:10:51,779
be the general disagreeable mood or something more specific,

195
00:10:51,780 --> 00:10:53,379
you have to remove (the inclination)

196
00:10:53,380 --> 00:10:55,349
or rather discern, and by discerning you

197
00:10:55,350 --> 00:10:59,739
remove it automatically, inclination towards resisting it.

198
00:10:59,740 --> 00:11:02,019
Towards trying to find the justification for it.

199
00:11:02,020 --> 00:11:04,389
Towards trying to find an explanation for it,

200
00:11:04,390 --> 00:11:06,129
towards psychologizing it.

201
00:11:06,130 --> 00:11:06,919
just any of those

202
00:11:06,920 --> 00:11:08,109
things are mechanism

203
00:11:08,110 --> 00:11:12,099
which you're trying to engage in, so to remove it, get rid of it.

204
00:11:12,100 --> 00:11:16,819
And the subtlest of them is neutral feeling

205
00:11:16,820 --> 00:11:19,049
when it's neither pleasant nor unpleasant.

206
00:11:19,050 --> 00:11:26,469
And that's when people give into distraction, delusion, indolence, laziness, mental heedlessness.

207
00:11:26,470 --> 00:11:33,669
So if you don't do any of those 3 things,

208
00:11:33,670 --> 00:11:35,389
you're not perpetuating craving.

209
00:11:35,390 --> 00:11:40,949
Q: And at the same time

210
00:11:40,950 --> 00:11:44,609
you could be able to

211
00:11:44,610 --> 00:11:47,009
feel, to be aware of your feelings.

212
00:11:47,010 --> 00:11:52,539
A: Yes, of course, to the extent they have arisen on their own.

213
00:11:52,540 --> 00:11:55,999
because feelings arise, having arisen, they cease on their own,

214
00:11:56,000 --> 00:11:56,379
you have no

215
00:11:56,380 --> 00:12:00,689
say in that.

216
00:12:00,690 --> 00:12:01,479
That's what mindfulness of feeling is,

217
00:12:01,480 --> 00:12:06,589
discerning the nature, basically.

218
00:12:06,590 --> 00:12:08,199
Knowing that they have arisen on their own

219
00:12:08,200 --> 00:12:13,669
this pleasant experience at the moment, arisen on its own basically. That's fine.

220
00:12:13,670 --> 00:12:21,079
You try to get rid of it because pleasure is craving? No, it doesn't. Leaning too much

221
00:12:21,080 --> 00:12:23,469
towards that pleasure, means craving,

222
00:12:23,470 --> 00:12:28,479
leaning away from the disagreeable, means craving.

223
00:12:28,480 --> 00:12:34,820
Leaning towards forgetfulness and distraction

224
00:12:36,130 --> 00:12:45,979
means craving, in the neutral feeling.

225
00:12:45,980 --> 00:12:50,839
Q: So being aware of those leanings towards feelings is the way?

226
00:12:50,840 --> 00:12:54,219
A: Yes, that's a good way to start.

227
00:12:54,220 --> 00:12:57,079
You can't be having, ''oh this is my craving''

228
00:12:57,080 --> 00:12:58,819
Craving is in your attitude,

229
00:12:58,820 --> 00:13:01,209
but you can bring it down so precisely

230
00:13:01,210 --> 00:13:02,859
whereby you'd see either

231
00:13:02,860 --> 00:13:05,959
the presence of suffering or the presence of

232
00:13:05,960 --> 00:13:07,959
the possibility to suffer.

233
00:13:07,960 --> 00:13:09,889
Any of those is generated by the

234
00:13:09,890 --> 00:13:10,539
amount of your leaning

235
00:13:10,540 --> 00:13:13,789
You're automatically generating

236
00:13:13,790 --> 00:13:15,809
possible liability to suffering,

237
00:13:15,810 --> 00:13:19,969
which is in itself, dukka.

238
00:13:19,970 --> 00:13:24,689
So you use that, to know whether you lean or not

239
00:13:24,690 --> 00:13:27,209
Recognition of how liable to suffering

240
00:13:27,210 --> 00:13:27,940
does this make you.

241
00:13:44,550 --> 00:13:49,639
Q: There is no method that can show you that.

242
00:13:49,640 --> 00:13:53,879
A: Of course not. Because method is on the level of

243
00:13:53,880 --> 00:13:56,139
almost like bodily action or certainly

244
00:13:56,140 --> 00:13:57,109
bodily perceptions that

245
00:13:57,110 --> 00:13:59,069
you're perceiving or going through

246
00:13:59,070 --> 00:14:04,549
some motions. We're talking about intentions behind your actions.

247
00:14:04,550 --> 00:14:05,289
So whatever the method you do

248
00:14:05,290 --> 00:14:07,530
you have to look at intention behind, which means method becomes redundant

249
00:14:08,380 --> 00:14:10,919
which means method is your Sila.

250
00:14:10,920 --> 00:14:12,609
Method is your sense restraint,

251
00:14:12,610 --> 00:14:15,869
that is closest method as you can get.

252
00:14:15,870 --> 00:14:17,570
Method is your moderation in eating.

253
00:14:38,690 --> 00:14:45,549
Q: There's no point in

254
00:14:45,550 --> 00:14:49,659
noting every movement of your mind, quickly write it down?

255
00:14:49,660 --> 00:14:54,779
A: It's completely misplaced, looking in the wrong place.

256
00:14:54,780 --> 00:14:55,249
Because you're not seeing

257
00:14:55,250 --> 00:14:57,379
your intention to note.

258
00:14:57,380 --> 00:15:00,529
You couldn't be noting your intention to note.

259
00:15:00,530 --> 00:15:02,799
Noting is an action which is already intended

260
00:15:02,800 --> 00:15:06,679
which is already leaned towards,

261
00:15:06,680 --> 00:15:08,719
and you're not seeing that.

262
00:15:08,720 --> 00:15:09,679
By not seeing that, no amount

263
00:15:09,680 --> 00:15:14,209
of engaging in that action reveals its nature, otherwise Buddha

264
00:15:14,210 --> 00:15:19,369
would have given the method and described in the suttas, when they did ask him what was the direct method,

265
00:15:19,370 --> 00:15:22,659
he said, ''a young man, develops faith, leaves

266
00:15:22,660 --> 00:15:23,389
his home, lives

267
00:15:23,390 --> 00:15:27,139
restrained by the rules of Patimokkha, practises sense restraint,

268
00:15:27,140 --> 00:15:28,959
sees the danger in the slightest fault

269
00:15:28,960 --> 00:15:29,899
moderation in eating,

270
00:15:29,900 --> 00:15:33,439
and devotes his time basically to wakefulness.

271
00:15:33,440 --> 00:15:41,639
First Watch of the night, 2nd watch of the night, 3rd watch of the night. then he understands rebirth has been destroyed.

272
00:15:41,640 --> 00:15:42,989
And I remember first time I read as a layman,

273
00:15:42,990 --> 00:15:45,119
I was also looking for a method, and I thought this was too general,

274
00:15:45,120 --> 00:15:45,719
why wouldn't he give you

275
00:15:45,720 --> 00:15:53,179
a particular recipe, how to become enlightened? Because there isn't any. This is the most particular

276
00:15:53,180 --> 00:15:55,779
you can get, if you are not seeing it in a direct matter

277
00:15:55,780 --> 00:15:58,339
just because of all the wrong views that are on top of it.

278
00:15:58,340 --> 00:16:00,709
So you need to meet that Buddha's instruction

279
00:16:00,710 --> 00:16:04,159
halfway basically, or even two-thirds of the way to

280
00:16:04,160 --> 00:16:06,269
start to make sense.

281
00:16:06,270 --> 00:16:07,839
but if a person don't change any of you

282
00:16:07,840 --> 00:16:18,759
and then they just add on top of their views, their notion of their practices, that's what you can get. Methods and modern Vipassana technique,

283
00:16:18,760 --> 00:16:21,869
or methods of concentration and so on

284
00:16:21,870 --> 00:16:23,939
No, you have to look at intention behind action

285
00:16:23,940 --> 00:16:25,599
so you can't concentrate on that,

286
00:16:25,600 --> 00:16:28,269
because it's behind your concentration.

287
00:16:28,270 --> 00:16:30,749
You can discern it, you can know it.

288
00:16:30,750 --> 00:16:31,329
That's why it says

289
00:16:31,330 --> 00:16:35,619
the consciousness is to be fully understood.

290
00:16:35,620 --> 00:16:36,770
Not concentrated on.

291
00:16:41,770 --> 00:16:45,319
Q: So you can't be aware of your Intentions?

292
00:16:45,320 --> 00:16:51,489
A: You can be aware, in that peripheral background manner, but awareness and concentration in terms of techniques

293
00:16:51,490 --> 00:16:53,409
is not the same thing.

294
00:16:53,410 --> 00:16:54,239
People are not aware

295
00:16:54,240 --> 00:16:57,979
when they do meditation techniques, quite opposite, they're practising some sort of

296
00:16:57,980 --> 00:17:00,309
focusing exercises on one thing or the other,

297
00:17:00,310 --> 00:17:15,029
which means there's no general awareness there.
Q: To be able to see your intentions?

298
00:17:15,030 --> 00:17:20,149
A: They can only be seen indirectly.

299
00:17:20,150 --> 00:17:23,019
Q: By the way you are,

300
00:17:23,020 --> 00:17:24,459
whatever you're choosing,

301
00:17:24,460 --> 00:17:25,549
A: They can only be seen indirectly

302
00:17:25,550 --> 00:17:31,939
on the basis of sense restraint and sila.

303
00:17:31,940 --> 00:17:36,540
You can't see them indirectly if you are unrestrained.

304
00:17:40,480 --> 00:17:44,580
Q: If you are not restrained by keeping sila?

305
00:17:50,780 --> 00:17:53,529
A: You can have a notion of it, to some extent

306
00:17:53,530 --> 00:17:57,629
but understanding the Nature, having that clarity

307
00:17:57,630 --> 00:17:59,549
generated to the point of being able to

308
00:17:59,550 --> 00:18:00,669
fully discern it,

309
00:18:00,670 --> 00:18:02,219
you won't have that.

310
00:18:02,220 --> 00:18:04,920
It is just like trying to collect the water

311
00:18:06,080 --> 00:18:08,799
in 10 meter deep pool, tank

312
00:18:08,800 --> 00:18:11,489
we just constantly punching hole in the bottom of it.

313
00:18:11,490 --> 00:18:15,399
So it'll never fill up to the top.

314
00:18:15,400 --> 00:18:16,089
And you need to have

315
00:18:16,090 --> 00:18:22,550
it filled up basically.